From d648e2f20fea725ffb124b46a50f3e1f99852e85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <c@local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:06:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Water/methanol injection (WMI): tank level, fault alert,
 timing and fuel while flowing

Requested by Carlos (next firmware round, 01/11).
- the WMI valve or pump is one of the 8 Generic PWM outputs (pin,
  frequency, MAP x RPM duty table, or on/off); wmiGppwmChannel picks it
- new module WaterMethanol:
  - tank low switch (wmiLevelPin, with a delay for slosh): turns the WMI
    output off so the pump does not run dry
  - status: off / ready / flowing (duty above wmiActiveDuty) / tank low /
    fault (WMI asked with the tank low)
  - timing added (wmiTimingAdd) and fuel change (wmiFuelTrim) while WMI
    flows, full value at 100 % duty, scaled by the duty
- new alert sensor 'WMI fault' (gppwm channel 48) so an alert can cut
  boost (safe mode) or warn; ve/afr blend axis label offset 48 -> 49
- live data: WMI duty, WMI status
- TunerStudio: Advanced > Water/methanol injection
- 4 new tests

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012qcg6EYkigZc99xZ8xdABd
